  "term": "Lioresal",
  "definition": "Lioresal is a brand name for baclofen, a muscle-relaxing drug used to reduce spasms linked to spinal cord injury and multiple sclerosis. It works by stimulating GABA-B receptors in the brain and spinal cord, which lowers excitatory nerve signaling.",
